From fdfffa064fbbdd1957bae5af5e5501a67a4ec6b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: littlemex <littlemex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:12:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(mvp): let a caller read its own billing rates and
 per-request cost

THE GAP

A caller that prices its own traffic needs two facts only this gateway holds:
the rate it bills each model at, and what it actually charged for a given
request. Neither is readable by an ordinary caller. `GET
/api/mvp/admin/pricing-config` requires `usage:read-all` (admin-only), and
`GET /api/mvp/me/usage-history` rows store `cost_microusd` and the request
id but return neither.

OBSERVED

tierbook derives a per-task-type assignment from observed token counts
priced at current rates, so that a price change alone re-derives it. Without
a readable rate table its candidate file has to carry a hand-copied price
list, which is the figure most likely to be wrong; and without per-request
cost and id there is no way to check the derived cost against the bill.

THE FIX

`GET /api/mvp/me/rates`, gated on the existing `usage:read-self` scope (the
one `/me/usage-summary` and `/me/usage-history` already require), returns the
rate table `mvp.pricing.effective_rates()` already serves to the admin view,
narrowed to the pricing keys reachable by models this caller is eligible for
via `mvp.eligibility.refusal_for` -- the same filter `GET /v1/models` applies.
No new price computation and no new eligibility rule. It is its own endpoint
rather than a field on either provider-specific models listing because one
pricing key can serve models on both wire protocols.

`/me/usage-history` entries now carry `cost_microusd` and `request_id`, the
id the gateway echoes as `x-sc-span-id`. `UsageLogsRepository.record()` also
writes `request_id` as its own attribute, so a reader need not parse the
`timestamp_log_id` sort key. Both fields are null, not zero, on rows that
predate the change or were never priced.

Delete this patch once it is upstream: when `GET /api/mvp/me/rates` exists
and usage-history rows carry `cost_microusd` and `request_id` on the pinned
commit.
